<title>USA: U.S. barley growers unhappy with Canada monitoring.</title>
<headline>U.S. barley growers unhappy with Canada monitoring.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. National Barley Growers Association said a U.S. decision announced Tuesday to start monitoring imports of Canadian barley would be ineffectual.</p>
<p>The U.S. Trade Representative and Agriculture Department said they would consider taking action if barley imports from Canada went above the 1993/94 levels.</p>
<p>But the barley growers association said barley imports from Canada were a record in 1993/94 because of flooding that disrupted the U.S. corn crop and said monitoring should be based on realistic import numbers.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8489</p>
